: \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4478, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:26\", \"token_count\": 1509, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Issue: Separate atomic operations for value and `isSet` flag can lead to inconsistent state\\n\\n- Potential solutions discussed:\\n\\n  - Use atomic pointer with combined value+set state\\n\\n  - David had tried this approach before but found it slower\\n\\n  - Need to investigate performance implications of different approaches\\n\\n### 3. Contrib Repository Items\\n\\n**Error recording for spans with semantic conventions:**\\n\\n- Discussion about when to record error.type attribute vs exception events\\n\\n- Related to Tyler's work on error type functions\\n\\n- Not blocking for current milestone but worth investigating\\n\\n### 4. Action Items\\n\\n- **Tyler:** \\n\\n  - Respond to issue with standardization feedback\\n\\n  - Review and provide feedback on PR #7443 race condition\\n\\n  - Continue work on error type handling improvements\\n\\n- **David:**\\n\\n  - Fix race condition in PR #7443 extrema implementation\\n\\n  - Review Prometheus error handling PR\\n\\n  - Continue work on lockless exponential histogram\\n\\n- **Bryan:**\\n\\n  - Review PR #7474 (exemplar reservoir optimization)\\n\\n  - Review PR #7443 (histogram optimization)\\n\\n### 5. Upcoming Events\\n\\n- KubeCon in ~3 weeks (November 8-9 for Maintainer Summit)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"issu separ atom oper for valu and isset flag can lead to inconsist state potenti solut discuss use atom pointer with combin valu set state david had tri this approach befor but found it slower need to investig perform implic of differ approach 3 contrib repositori item error record for span with semant convent discuss about when to record error type attribut v except event relat to tyler s work on error type function not block for current mileston but worth investig 4 action item tyler respond to issu with standard feedback review and provid feedback on pr 7443 race condit continu work on error type handl improv david fix race condit in pr 7443 extremum implement review prometheus error handl pr continu work on lockless exponenti histogram bryan review pr 7474 exemplar reservoir optim review pr 7443 histogram optim 5 upcom event kubecon in 3 week novemb 89 for maintain summit\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073509be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"id\": \"322dbd9fa8f7866f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27358086651460667, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10655545359229524, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66330683, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073509be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3423, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:26\", \"token_count\": 796, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"*   David also mentioned ongoing work on exponential histograms and a simpler \\\"last value\\\" PR that shares code with the histogram one.\\n\\n*   Tyler expressed a strong desire to merge the histogram reservoir PR in the current milestone due to its significant performance improvement and encouraged attendees to review it.\\n\\n**6. Milestone Check-in and Release Goals**\\n\\n*   Tyler conducted a check-in on the v1.39.0 milestones for [Otel](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/milestone/74) and [Contrib](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/milestone/33).\\n\\n*   **Exposed Temporality Selector Function PR:** Tyler noted that a previous SIG meeting concluded this PR was API pollution and should be closed. He will draft a comment and close it today.\\n\\n*   **Simple Span Processor (Tracing):** This PR needs another round of reviews but is considered straightforward and should remain in the milestone.\\n\\n*   **OTLP Metric GRPC Exporter Metrics:** This PR has been open for a while and needs more iteration. It might be moved out of the current milestone if a release push occurs.\\n\\n*   **Metrics SDK Standard Out Metrics Exporter & Standard Log Exporter:** Both PRs lack follow-up from their original authors and significant work is still needed. They are candidates for being bumped from the milestone.\\n\\n*   **Overall Release Strategy:** Tyler proposed making a release before KubeCon (less than a month away) and urged everyone to prioritize reviews for the critical PRs to achieve this goal.\\n\\n**7. KubeCon Discussion**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** asked if there was anything specific to announce or discuss at KubeCon.\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** mentioned the extended attributes merge in specification and product as something he'd like to highlight, though it's not ready.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** expressed interest in showcasing the new observability features.\\n\\n*   David suggested working towards a stable release of the HTTP instrumentation in Contrib. Tyler agreed it was a good idea but noted the significant work involved due to existing \\\"cruft\\\" and potential needs for API restructuring.\\n\\n**8. Tyler's Side Project (OTLP Exporter Error Types)**\\n\\n*   Tyler shared that he's been working on introducing new, custom error types for OTLP exporters to provide clearer, more unified error messages. This involves distinguishing between HTTP/gRPC errors, partial errors, and warnings. He has a prototype integrated for Otel Trace gRPC. While not critical, it improves observability and user understanding of errors.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"david also mention ongo work on exponenti histogram and a simpler last valu pr that share code with the histogram one tyler express a strong desir to merg the histogram reservoir pr in the current mileston due to it signific perform improv and encourag attende to review it 6 mileston check in and releas goal tyler conduct a check in on the v1 39 0 mileston for otel http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go mileston 74 and contrib http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib mileston 33 expos tempor selector function pr tyler note that a previous sig meet conclud this pr wa api pollut and should be close he will draft a comment and close it today simpl span processor trace this pr need anoth round of review but is consid straightforward and should remain in the mileston otlp metric grpc export metric this pr ha been open for a while and need more iter it might be move out of the current mileston if a releas push occur metric sdk standard out metric export standard log export both pr lack follow up from their origin author and signific work is still need they are candid for be bump from the mileston overal releas strategi tyler propos make a releas befor kubecon less than a month away and urg everyon to priorit review for the critic pr to achiev this goal 7 kubecon discuss david ashpol ask if there wa anyth specif to announc or discus at kubecon robert paj ą k mention the extend attribut merg in specif and product a someth he d like to highlight though it s not readi tyler yahn express interest in showcas the new observ featur david suggest work toward a stabl releas of the http instrument in contrib tyler agre it wa a good idea but note the signific work involv due to exist cruft and potenti need for api restructur 8 tyler s side project otlp export error type tyler share that he s been work on introduc new custom error type for otlp export to provid clearer more unifi error messag this involv distinguish between http grpc error partial error and warn he ha a prototyp integr for otel trace grpc while not critic it improv observ and user understand of error\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"1bed9e41a9b05e24\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2731688826368096, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09383611805258515, \"vector_similarity\": 0.691612, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Improve performance of histogram `Record` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric` when min and max are disabled using `NoMinMax`. (#7306)\\n\\n- Improve error handling for dropped data during translation by using `prometheus.NewInvalidMetric` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus`. ⚠️ **Breaking Change:** Previously, these cases were only logged and scrapes succeeded. Now, when translation would drop data (e.g., invalid label/value), the exporter emits a `NewInvalidMetric`, and Prometheus scrapes **fail with HTTP 500** by default. To preserve the prior behavior (scrapes succeed while errors are logged), configure your Prometheus HTTP handler with: `promhttp.HandlerOpts{ ErrorHandling: promhttp.ContinueOnError }`. (#7363)\\n\\n- Replace fnv hash with xxhash in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute` for better performance. (#7371)\\n\\n- The default `TranslationStrategy` in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/prometheus` is changed from `otlptranslator.NoUTF8EscapingWithSuffixes` to `otlptranslator.UnderscoreEscapingWithSuffixes`. (#7421)\\n\\n- Improve performance of concurrent measurements in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7427)\\n\\n- Include W3C TraceFlags (bits 0–7) in the OTLP `Span.Flags` field in `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp` and `go.opentelemetry.io/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc`. (#7438)\\n\\n- The `ErrorType` function in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.37.0` now handles custom error types.\\n\\n  If an error implements an `ErrorType() string` method, the return value of that method will be used as the error type. (#7442)\\n\\n### Fixed\\n\\n- Fix `WithInstrumentationAttributes` options in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log` to properly merge attributes when passed multiple times instead of replacing them. Attributes with duplicate keys will use the last value passed. (#7300)\\n\\n- The equality of `attribute.Set` when using the `Equal` method is not affected by the user overriding the empty set pointed to by `attribute.EmptySet` in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/attribute`. (#7357)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"improv perform of histogram record in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric when min and max are disabl use nominmax 7306 improv error handl for drop data dure translat by use prometheus newinvalidmetr in go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus break chang previous these case were onli log and scrape succeed now when translat would drop data e g invalid label valu the export emit a 