: \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"0760475a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:48\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455)\\n\\n*   **Bryan Boreham** questioned the relevance to OpenTelemetry, to which Damien clarified it's for instrumenting file uploads via the HTTP server.\\n\\n*   The discussion revolved around implementing an automatic cleanup mechanism for these temporary files. Proposed solutions included:\\n\\n    *   Option 1: `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`\\n\\n    *   Option 2: Leave it to the user to decide (\\\"whoever uses it is responsible for cleanup\\\")\\n\\n    *   Option 3: Provide a configurable option with a default.\\n\\n*   Damien suggested starting with automatic deletion without an explicit option, adding one only if a strong need arises. The notes from the agenda suggested starting with default behavior of removal, waiting for user interest to add configuration, and empowering component owners to make this decision.\\n\\n*   Tyler acknowledged that the instrumentation is responsible for cleanup and that this issue needs to be addressed.\\n\\n**3. Long-seen Code Owners/Triagers Check-in**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** reported that Chengzhen (Scorpion Knives), a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho, has had no GitHub activity since February and is the sole owner for otelecho.\\n\\n*   Damien pinged Chengzhen on Slack today and will wait a couple of weeks for a response. If there's no response, he plans to propose moving Chengzhen to Emeritus status due to inactivity.\\n\\n**4. Robert Pająk's PR (Parsing Algorithm)**\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** asked Tyler if his PR ([sdk/log: Fix AddAttributes, SetAttributes, SetBody on Record to not mutate input #7403](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7403)) needed Tyler's specific review or if another approval would suffice to unblock it.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** encouraged others to review and stated that the project shouldn't be blocked waiting for him, though he would try to review it within a few days.\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** offered to review the PR. The goal is to merge it into the current milestone.\\n\\n**5. David Ashpole's PRs (Metrics SDK Optimizations)**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** provided an update on his histogram reservoir optimization PR. He explained that fixing a race condition initially worsened performance, making it equivalent to using a lock. The new approach involves one lock per measurement instead of one for the whole reservoir, resulting in a 3x-4x performance improvement. The PR is now much simpler and mostly involves concurrent safety testing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 74455 http github com golang go issu 74455 bryan boreham question the relev to opentelemetri to which damien clarifi it s for instrument file upload via the http server the discuss revolv around implement an automat cleanup mechan for these temporari file propos solut includ option 1 c request multipartform removeal option 2 leav it to the user to decid whoever us it is respons for cleanup option 3 provid a configur option with a default damien suggest start with automat delet without an explicit option ad one onli if a strong need aris the note from the agenda suggest start with default behavior of remov wait for user interest to add configur and empow compon owner to make this decis tyler acknowledg that the instrument is respons for cleanup and that this issu need to be address 3 long seen code owner triager check in damien mathieu report that chengzhen scorpion knife a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho ha had no github activ sinc februari and is the sole owner for otelecho damien ping chengzhen on slack today and will wait a coupl of week for a respons if there s no respons he plan to propos move chengzhen to emeritus status due to inact 4 robert paj ą k s pr pars algorithm robert paj ą k ask tyler if his pr sdk log fix addattribut setattribut setbodi on record to not mutat input 7403 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7403 need tyler s specif review or if anoth approv would suffic to unblock it tyler yahn encourag other to review and state that the project shouldn t be block wait for him though he would tri to review it within a few day david ashpol offer to review the pr the goal is to merg it into the current mileston 5 david ashpol s pr metric sdk optim david ashpol provid an updat on his histogram reservoir optim pr he explain that fix a race condit initi worsen perform make it equival to use a lock the new approach involv one lock per measur instead of one for the whole reservoir result in a 3x 4x perform improv the pr is now much simpler and most involv concurr safeti test\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"287e2a602b3808f0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2566983162478538, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07506889463979112, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6805003, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073913c48a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1c03168edc496741\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2547548506552165, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06255741236459508, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70321554, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073913c48a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:22\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"entry-3390010099 temporality selector custom parsing configuration rejected full OpenTelemetry configuration file format\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"No. Custom temporality-selector parsing/configuration was rejected for the Go SDK; users were directed to the full OpenTelemetry configuration-file format instead. (`SRC-NOTE-03`)\n\nOpenTelemetry Go `v1.39.0` did ship selector functions in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`: `DeltaTemporalitySelector`, `CumulativeTemporalitySelector`, and `LowMemoryTemporalitySelector` (PR #7434). (`SRC-REL-01`)"}}
